# SA-EP-002 — Enterprise Service Catalog

**Project:** BTA V5.1 — HCGO Enterprise Service Architecture

**Status:** Approved

**Classification:** Enterprise Service Architecture

---

# Purpose

Establish the authoritative architectural inventory of Enterprise Services across HCGO.

The Enterprise Service Catalog faithfully inventories the Enterprise Services that expose approved Enterprise Capabilities while preserving enterprise authority, ownership, stewardship, governance, lifecycle authority, traceability, and enterprise semantics.

The Enterprise Service Catalog is an architectural artifact.

It is not a technology implementation artifact.

---

# Architecture Objective

Establish the authoritative Enterprise Service Catalog for HCGO.

The Enterprise Service Catalog is the authoritative architectural inventory of Enterprise Services that expose approved Enterprise Capabilities across HCGO.

It faithfully represents Enterprise Capability Architecture without introducing implementation concerns.

Enterprise Services remain independent of APIs, runtime implementation, messaging, protocols, databases, or implementation technologies.

---

# Enterprise Service Catalog

The Enterprise Service Catalog shall identify:

- Enterprise Service Name
- Enterprise Capability Exposed
- Enterprise Service Purpose
- Authoritative Enterprise Capability
- Enterprise Service Steward
- Enterprise Service Classification
- Enterprise Service Responsibilities
- Enterprise Service Relationships
- Enterprise Service Boundaries
- Enterprise Service Consumers
- Enterprise Service Governance

For every Enterprise Service identify:

- Service Name
- Enterprise Capability Exposed
- Purpose
- Authoritative Enterprise Capability
- Steward
- Responsibilities
- Authorized Consumers
- Enterprise Relationships
- Enterprise Boundaries
- Governance Notes

---

# The Enterprise Service Catalog Shall NOT Identify

The Enterprise Service Catalog shall not identify:

- REST APIs
- FastAPI Endpoints
- HTTP Methods
- URLs
- GraphQL
- gRPC
- Messaging
- Runtime Execution
- Service Implementation
- Database Implementation
- Technology Implementation

Those responsibilities belong to the Technology Implementation phase.

---

# Enterprise Service Boundary Preservation

Enterprise Services shall expose Enterprise Capabilities while preserving:

- Capability Boundaries
- Ownership Boundaries
- Stewardship Boundaries
- Governance Boundaries
- Information Boundaries

Enterprise Services shall never collapse or bypass these enterprise boundaries.

---

# Enterprise Principle

Every Enterprise Service shall expose one authoritative Enterprise Capability.

Enterprise Services faithfully expose Enterprise Capability responsibilities.

Enterprise Services shall never redefine:

- Enterprise Authority
- Enterprise Ownership
- Enterprise Stewardship
- Enterprise Governance
- Enterprise Lifecycle Authority
- Enterprise Semantics

Enterprise Services remain architectural representations of Enterprise Capabilities.

---

# Enterprise Capability Ownership Preservation

The Enterprise Service Catalog shall identify Enterprise Services.

It shall not redefine Enterprise Capabilities.

Each Enterprise Service shall trace directly to one authoritative Enterprise Capability.

Enterprise Capability ownership, authority, stewardship, governance, lifecycle authority, and enterprise semantics remain vested in the owning Enterprise Capability.

The Enterprise Service Catalog faithfully inventories the Enterprise Services that expose those responsibilities.

---

# Architectural Rationale

Throughout Constitutional Governance, Enterprise Discovery, Enterprise Analysis, Enterprise Persistence Architecture, and Enterprise Service Architecture, HCGO has consistently distinguished between enterprise responsibilities and the architectural representations of those responsibilities.

Enterprise Capabilities define enterprise responsibilities.

Enterprise Services expose enterprise responsibilities.

The Enterprise Service Catalog inventories Enterprise Services.

The catalog therefore represents Enterprise Service Architecture rather than Enterprise Capability Architecture.

This preserves the constitutional separation between:

- Enterprise Capability
- Enterprise Service
- Enterprise Service Catalog
- Technology Implementation

Each architectural layer has a unique constitutional responsibility.

The Enterprise Capability remains the authoritative enterprise responsibility.

The Enterprise Service remains the architectural exposure of that responsibility.

The Enterprise Service Catalog remains the authoritative architectural inventory of those Enterprise Services.

Technology faithfully implements the Enterprise Service Catalog.

At no point does architectural inventory transfer enterprise authority.

---

# Constitutional Principle

Architectural inventory never transfers enterprise authority.

Enterprise Capabilities remain the constitutional source of enterprise responsibility.

Enterprise Services faithfully expose those responsibilities.

The Enterprise Service Catalog faithfully inventories those Enterprise Services.

Technology faithfully implements the Enterprise Service Catalog.

Neither architectural representation nor architectural inventory may redefine:

- Enterprise Authority
- Enterprise Ownership
- Enterprise Stewardship
- Enterprise Governance
- Enterprise Lifecycle Authority
- Enterprise Semantics

---

# Architecture Outcome

The Enterprise Service Catalog becomes the authoritative architectural inventory of Enterprise Services across HCGO.

Every Enterprise Service shall trace directly to one authoritative Enterprise Capability.

Every Enterprise Capability may expose one or more Enterprise Services as approved through Enterprise Architecture.

All Enterprise Service artifacts shall faithfully conform to the Enterprise Service Catalog.

Technology implementations shall faithfully implement the Enterprise Service Catalog without redefining:

- Enterprise Capabilities
- Enterprise Services
- Enterprise Authority
- Enterprise Ownership
- Enterprise Stewardship
- Enterprise Governance
- Enterprise Lifecycle Authority
- Enterprise Traceability
- Enterprise Semantics

The Enterprise Service Catalog therefore becomes the authoritative architectural bridge between Enterprise Capability Architecture and Technology Implementation.

---

